WEBVTT

00:01.372 --> 00:04.881
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.882 --> 00:08.146
<i>♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on T.V. ♪</i>

00:08.147 --> 00:11.795
<i>♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.796 --> 00:14.798
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.799 --> 00:18.301
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.302 --> 00:21.571
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.572 --> 00:23.140
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.141 --> 00:24.875
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.876 --> 00:29.876
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:35.553 --> 00:38.321
- Peter, you're not even dressed.
- For what?

00:38.322 --> 00:40.490
Chris's class is performing
a rock and roll choir.

00:40.491 --> 00:42.325
They've been practicing for months.

00:42.326 --> 00:44.327
"For months," or "four months"?

00:44.328 --> 00:46.163
For months. Three months.

00:46.164 --> 00:47.831
Not long enough. Pass.

00:47.832 --> 00:49.366
I just wish we were doing songs

00:49.367 --> 00:52.169
that weren't so hard to sing as a group.

00:52.170 --> 00:54.271
<i>♪ Six o'clock, TV hours, don't
get caught in foreign tower ♪</i>

00:54.272 --> 00:56.673
<i>♪ Slash and burn, return,
listen to yourself churn ♪</i>

00:56.674 --> 00:58.742
<i>♪ Lock him in uniform and
book burning, bloodletting ♪</i>

00:58.743 --> 01:00.677
<i>♪ Leonard Bernstein ♪</i>

01:00.678 --> 01:02.879
<i>♪ Birthday party, cheesecake,
jelly bean, boom... ♪</i>

01:02.880 --> 01:05.582
- How was it?
- Terrible.

01:05.583 --> 01:08.018
<i>We now return to a 1980s movie</i>

01:08.019 --> 01:09.452
<i>you remember fondly,</i>

01:09.453 --> 01:11.388
<i>but now feels excruciatingly slow.</i>

01:11.389 --> 01:12.556
<i>All right, Stripes.</i>

01:12.557 --> 01:14.191
Ah, this was hilarious.

01:14.192 --> 01:16.126
All right, Bill Murray's driving a cab.

01:16.127 --> 01:18.061
Still driving a cab.

01:18.062 --> 01:20.197
Shot of the town.

01:20.198 --> 01:23.033
Going over a bridge.

01:23.034 --> 01:24.634
Traffic's neither heavy nor light.

01:24.635 --> 01:26.303
Get in the Army!

01:26.304 --> 01:28.305
I hope you don't plan
on just lying on the couch

01:28.306 --> 01:30.240
and watching TV all weekend.

01:30.241 --> 01:32.108
That's exactly what I plan to do.

01:32.109 --> 01:34.244
It's a free premium channel
preview weekend.

01:34.245 --> 01:35.812
Even Cinemax.

01:35.813 --> 01:38.548
One of the shows is actually
two boobs fighting.

01:38.549 --> 01:40.450
Sadly, there's still no penetration.

01:40.451 --> 01:42.452
Well, just expect me to do

01:42.453 --> 01:44.921
a lot of sour-faced,
arms-folded head shaking.

01:46.257 --> 01:47.958
Well, in return,

01:47.959 --> 01:50.260
you'll get a lot of
beaten-down husband eye-rolls.

01:56.567 --> 01:57.968
One of the neighbors called about

01:57.969 --> 02:00.837
a passive-aggressive domestic dispute.

02:00.838 --> 02:02.505
<i>Ooh, is that Stripes?</i>

02:02.506 --> 02:05.008
Eh, he's not in the Army yet.

02:06.844 --> 02:08.345
Peter, this is ridiculous.

02:08.346 --> 02:09.980
You've been lying here all weekend.

02:09.981 --> 02:12.415
I'm not bringing you any more food.

02:12.416 --> 02:14.484
I don't need you to.
I got a thousand dollar credit

02:14.485 --> 02:17.020
from Uber Eats 'cause
that driver pinched my bottom.

02:17.021 --> 02:20.290
Okay, well if you don't get up,
I won't have sex with you.

02:20.291 --> 02:22.459
And that will be different how...?

02:22.460 --> 02:24.828
And I'm still married to you because...?

02:25.997 --> 02:29.199
Guys, second time this week.

02:33.771 --> 02:35.505
Peter, you got to come outside.

02:35.506 --> 02:37.340
We found a used condom on the sidewalk.

02:37.341 --> 02:39.542
That's a bigger deal
than regular garbage.

02:39.543 --> 02:41.611
Ribbed. A woman was pleased with it.

02:41.612 --> 02:42.779
You got to see this, Peter.

02:42.780 --> 02:43.947
A used condom.

02:43.948 --> 02:45.048
Just right out here.

02:45.049 --> 02:46.616
And there's panties nearby.

02:46.617 --> 02:47.684
Joe, you're a cop.

02:47.685 --> 02:48.785
What do you think happened here?

02:48.786 --> 02:50.120
I'll tell you what happened.

02:50.121 --> 02:51.788
Somebody did it.

02:51.789 --> 02:53.657
Yeah!

02:53.658 --> 02:55.492
Peter, come out here and high five us

02:55.493 --> 02:57.294
over the sex someone else had.

02:57.295 --> 02:58.962
Someone had sex?

02:58.963 --> 03:01.731
I got to touch another guy's
hand to celebrate.

03:14.845 --> 03:17.948
<i>Oh, now he gets to the Army.</i>

03:20.518 --> 03:22.686
Hmm. I've seen this before.

03:22.687 --> 03:25.155
It's from Ethan Allen,
if I'm not mistaken.

03:25.156 --> 03:27.357
- Am I gonna be okay?
- You'll be fine.

03:27.358 --> 03:29.592
Here's a video to help you understand.

03:33.164 --> 03:36.866
<i>Hi, I'm Oliver Platt, and I'm
currently fused to this chair.</i>

03:36.867 --> 03:38.435
<i>But how does it happen?</i>

03:38.436 --> 03:40.103
<i>When a fat guy's sweaty skin</i>

03:40.104 --> 03:41.604
<i>presses against couch fabric</i>

03:41.605 --> 03:43.373
for an extended period of time,

03:43.374 --> 03:46.509
<i>the fabric fibers
fuse together with the skin.</i>

03:46.510 --> 03:50.013
<i>The longer you stay sedentary,
the stronger the bond.</i>

03:50.014 --> 03:51.381
<i>My advice: relax.</i>

03:51.382 --> 03:52.949
<i>It's not the end of the world.</i>

03:52.950 --> 03:55.352
<i>Being fused to furniture
hasn't stopped me</i>

03:55.353 --> 03:57.187
<i>from being an adult with a child's name.</i>

03:57.188 --> 04:00.190
<i>And having thicker hair than a werewolf.</i>

04:00.191 --> 04:02.859
The procedure is called
"Rip You Off Real Fast."

04:02.860 --> 04:04.861
Very painful. Ready?

04:04.862 --> 04:07.097
Actually, I've decided
to keep the couch on me.

04:07.098 --> 04:08.865
Really? Are you sure?

04:08.866 --> 04:10.433
Oh, yeah. This is nothing.

04:10.434 --> 04:11.968
I've been in uncomfortable
situations before.

04:11.969 --> 04:14.804
Like, whenever I meet famous people.

04:14.805 --> 04:17.774
Hey, what's up? I'm Snoop Dogg,
know what I'm saying?

04:17.775 --> 04:19.376
I do.

04:19.377 --> 04:22.212
<i>But you don't, Peter, you don't.</i>

04:25.983 --> 04:27.650
How is it? Is-a good?

04:27.651 --> 04:28.752
Eh, it's a little tight.

04:28.753 --> 04:30.320
A little tight in-a the couch?

04:30.321 --> 04:32.088
Yeah, it's a little tight in the couch.

04:32.089 --> 04:33.556
Hey, what's it like going through life

04:33.557 --> 04:34.958
holding needles in your lips?

04:34.959 --> 04:36.393
Is-a not easy.

04:36.394 --> 04:38.061
Some-a time-a the needle,
they poke-a my lip,

04:38.062 --> 04:39.629
and I say-a, "Mamma mia!"

04:39.630 --> 04:41.498
Well, you still got
James Brolin coming in here,

04:41.499 --> 04:42.599
autographing your photos.

04:42.600 --> 04:43.767
That's kind of cool.

04:43.768 --> 04:45.068
You want to know something, a-Peter?

04:45.069 --> 04:46.436
He no come in here.

04:46.437 --> 04:49.005
I take-a the photo
from the dry cleaner's.

04:49.006 --> 04:50.473
Mamma mia, what a day.

04:50.474 --> 04:51.975
And now to say good night

04:51.976 --> 04:55.078
to all-a my celebrity pictures
on-a the wall.

04:55.079 --> 04:57.013
<i>Buona notte, Christopher Plummer.</i>

04:57.014 --> 05:00.116
Sleep-a with the angels,
Sherman-a Hemsley.

05:00.117 --> 05:02.752
See you when-a the sun shine, Ken Ober.

05:02.753 --> 05:06.156
And now, to say good night
to my favorite-a celebrity,

05:06.157 --> 05:08.691
James-a Brol... mamma mia!

05:08.692 --> 05:10.527
Who steal-a my James Brolin?

05:10.528 --> 05:13.096
I take-a that photo from the bakery.

05:13.097 --> 05:15.532
Pasta fazool,
what a good day in-a the bakery.

05:15.533 --> 05:17.333
You take-a good care of the place

05:17.334 --> 05:19.302
while I'm-a gone, William-a Katt.

05:19.303 --> 05:24.240
That goes a-double for you,
James-a Brol... mamma mia!

05:28.045 --> 05:29.979
Uh, hey, Mom?

05:29.980 --> 05:33.616
Was I always able to see the
living room from the kitchen?

05:33.617 --> 05:35.318
I've had enough of this.

05:35.319 --> 05:37.787
That stupid couch
is messing up our house.

05:37.788 --> 05:39.622
If Peter won't let
Dr. Hartman remove it,

05:39.623 --> 05:41.224
we're doing it ourselves.

05:41.225 --> 05:43.827
I put an Ambien in his beer,
so he's out cold.

05:43.828 --> 05:46.062
<i>I saw you put Ambien in your beer, too.</i>

05:46.063 --> 05:48.731
Every adult has
to take Ambien every night

05:48.732 --> 05:51.367
to even have a prayer at sleep.

05:54.805 --> 05:56.973
All right, kids,
we're gonna use these scissors

05:56.974 --> 05:59.809
to separate your father from the couch.

05:59.810 --> 06:01.711
I can't tell skin from couch.

06:01.712 --> 06:03.213
Well, err on the skin side.

06:03.214 --> 06:05.014
I love this couch.

06:05.015 --> 06:06.916
It's from Ethan Allen, you know.

06:10.387 --> 06:12.222
Wha...?

06:12.223 --> 06:13.823
W-What-what's going on?

06:13.824 --> 06:16.493
Peter, enough is enough,
that couch is coming off.

06:16.494 --> 06:18.394
We're sick of your shenanigans.

06:18.395 --> 06:20.730
How dare you?

06:20.731 --> 06:23.166
I work my ass off to bring home
the bacon for this family,

06:23.167 --> 06:25.034
and all you can say is,
"We don't want bacon,

06:25.035 --> 06:26.669
we want actual money!"

06:26.670 --> 06:29.506
Well, I don't have money,
I spent it all on bacon!

06:29.507 --> 06:31.341
Peter, put yourself in our shoes.

06:31.342 --> 06:34.010
I can't. My feet swelled up
too much from all the bacon.

06:34.011 --> 06:35.879
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm going to sleep

06:35.880 --> 06:37.614
on the couch on the couch.

06:57.601 --> 06:59.636
Chris, give me a hand with this.

06:59.637 --> 07:01.271
All right, you ready?

07:01.272 --> 07:03.973
All right, one, two, three.

07:03.974 --> 07:05.575
- Okay, uh, easy, easy, easy...
- Uh... uh...

07:05.576 --> 07:07.410
- Easy, easy, easy, easy, easy.
- Okay, all right.

07:07.411 --> 07:08.811
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa. Stop,
stop, stop, stop, stop, stop.

07:08.812 --> 07:10.280
- Stop, stop.
- What? What?

07:10.281 --> 07:12.248
- No, no, no, no, no. Twist it.
- What? I am.

07:12.249 --> 07:14.150
Just look down, all right?
Just-just look at me,

07:14.151 --> 07:15.985
look what I'm doing. All right,
see the way I'm twisting it?

07:15.986 --> 07:18.321
- Okay, ju... No, no, no, no, no.
- Okay. Wait... what?

07:18.322 --> 07:20.456
You know what? All right, just...
Hang... just put-put it down.

07:20.457 --> 07:22.559
- Put it down. Just drop it, drop it.
- All right. All right.

07:22.560 --> 07:26.129
All right, let's... Let's just
hang on and figure this out.

07:26.130 --> 07:28.231
All-all right, okay.

07:28.232 --> 07:30.066
All right. Okay. I-I got it.
I know what we're gonna...

07:30.067 --> 07:31.668
Okay, okay. All right, y-you...
We... here's what we're gonna do,

07:31.669 --> 07:33.303
We're gonna take the cushions off,

07:33.304 --> 07:35.405
unscrew the legs, take the mattress out,

07:35.406 --> 07:37.273
and this whole thing's
gonna be a lot simpler.

07:37.274 --> 07:39.642
It's easier than we're making it.

07:39.643 --> 07:41.611
This isn't working.

07:41.612 --> 07:43.346
You know what? Just give me a push.

07:54.592 --> 07:56.092
I have some bad news.

07:56.093 --> 07:58.761
Ethan survived,
but Allen didn't make it.

07:58.762 --> 08:00.663
- What about Peter?
- Oh, him.

08:00.664 --> 08:02.665
He's in what we call a comma.

08:02.666 --> 08:04.000
Now, where's his chart?

08:04.001 --> 08:06.836
Ah, here it is. "Griffin coma Peter."

08:06.837 --> 08:08.838
Will he ever recover?

08:08.839 --> 08:10.540
How long is he gonna be like this?

08:10.541 --> 08:13.042
Please tell me he's gonna be okay...

08:25.456 --> 08:26.723
Oh, God.

08:36.500 --> 08:38.067
God?

08:38.068 --> 08:39.135
Yes.

08:39.136 --> 08:40.670
And no Trump questions.

08:40.671 --> 08:42.338
Okay.

08:43.540 --> 08:45.742
I have nothing else to ask you.

08:51.987 --> 08:54.989
I can't believe I'm stuck
in an elevator with God.

08:54.990 --> 08:57.792
Although, I guess you are
everywhere, and in all places.

08:57.793 --> 08:59.060
No, you're thinking of Kevin Hart.

08:59.061 --> 09:00.261
Ha! I know, right?

09:00.262 --> 09:01.329
I-In every movie.

09:01.330 --> 09:02.397
Him and The Rock.

09:02.398 --> 09:03.664
Oh, I love The Rock.

09:03.665 --> 09:05.233
No, no, no, I love The Rock, too.

09:05.234 --> 09:07.769
He's just-he's just in a lot of stuff.

09:07.770 --> 09:09.437
You know, his real name
is Dwayne Johnson.

09:09.438 --> 09:10.705
Yeah, I know.

09:10.706 --> 09:12.273
<i>We have Us Weekly on Earth, too.</i>

09:12.274 --> 09:14.242
Wait, why are you here?

09:14.243 --> 09:15.643
Shouldn't you be up in heaven?

09:15.644 --> 09:16.744
There was an issue.

09:16.745 --> 09:18.413
Uh, a-a few angels came forward.

09:18.414 --> 09:20.581
I don't remember things
exactly as they do,

09:20.582 --> 09:24.018
but I respect their experience.

09:24.019 --> 09:25.820
How did I get here?

09:25.821 --> 09:27.622
Well, you had a couch
attached to your back,

09:27.623 --> 09:30.291
and you fell down the stairs
and hit your head pretty hard.

09:30.292 --> 09:31.793
<i>Am I in a Leftovers?</i>

09:31.794 --> 09:32.960
<i>Is this a Leftovers?</i>

09:32.961 --> 09:34.462
I don't know what that is.

09:34.463 --> 09:37.532
It was an HBO show starring
a bottle of hair dye.

09:38.600 --> 09:40.334
Man, this thing is really stuck.

09:40.335 --> 09:42.870
Hey, can you use
your God powers to get us out?

09:42.871 --> 09:44.372
No, they don't really work in elevators.

09:44.373 --> 09:45.606
Kind of like a cell phone.

09:45.607 --> 09:46.774
I don't have a signal.

09:46.775 --> 09:47.809
I have a cell phone.

09:47.810 --> 09:48.943
It's silver.

09:48.944 --> 09:50.912
That's rad, Peter.

09:52.781 --> 09:56.184
I always dreamed of being stuck
in an elevator with Tom Brady.

09:56.185 --> 09:57.718
That makes two of us.

09:57.719 --> 09:59.854
Can I ask you my Tom Brady questions?

09:59.855 --> 10:02.023
I wouldn't deign to speak for Tom Brady.

10:02.024 --> 10:04.559
Understood, understood.

10:04.560 --> 10:07.728
- Hey, do atheists go to hell?
- No.

10:07.729 --> 10:09.730
How about people who say
they are not religious,

10:09.731 --> 10:11.466
but they are spiritual?

10:11.467 --> 10:13.167
Straight to hell,
to the boiler room of hell.

10:13.168 --> 10:15.002
All the way down.

10:15.003 --> 10:16.337
Sometimes, I pull them out

10:16.338 --> 10:17.705
just so they think everything
is gonna be okay,

10:17.706 --> 10:19.373
but then, I put them right back in.

10:19.374 --> 10:21.075
Good, good.

10:21.076 --> 10:22.910
That makes me happy.

10:22.911 --> 10:26.247
Um, God, here's something
you might be able to tell me.

10:26.248 --> 10:27.849
Will Taylor Swift and Katy Perry

10:27.850 --> 10:31.819
ever reconcile their differences?

10:31.820 --> 10:33.154
What are you looking for?

10:33.155 --> 10:34.989
Oh, I'm sorry,
I'm looking for the gay guy

10:34.990 --> 10:36.390
who can answer that one.

10:38.327 --> 10:41.195
Some people say we're just
a computer simulation

10:41.196 --> 10:43.030
run by a higher species.

10:43.031 --> 10:45.199
- Is that true?
- It is.

10:47.703 --> 10:49.237
My guy sucks.

10:49.238 --> 10:51.272
Want to trade guys for a little while?

10:51.273 --> 10:53.207
Oh, never mind.

10:53.208 --> 10:56.511
I'll stick with this pile
of crap I already have.

10:56.512 --> 11:00.181
<i>All right, can you name every
SNL actor alphabetically?</i>

11:00.182 --> 11:02.416
- Alphabetically by last name?
- Yes.

11:02.417 --> 11:04.519
- And no featured players?
- Yeah, okay.

11:04.520 --> 11:07.889
Fred Armisen, Dan Aykroyd,
Morwenna Banks, Vanessa Bayer...

11:07.890 --> 11:10.358
Jon Lovitz, Norm Macdonald,
Gail Matthius...

11:10.359 --> 11:11.692
Gail Matthius, good pull.

11:11.693 --> 11:13.561
Michael McKean, Mark McKinney...

11:13.562 --> 11:17.064
Nancy Walls, Kristen Wiig,
and Sasheer Zamata.

11:17.065 --> 11:19.534
<i>Wow. Now do Kids in the Hall.</i>

11:19.535 --> 11:21.369
That was five guys, Peter.

11:21.370 --> 11:23.004
- Name 'em.
- I can't.

11:24.640 --> 11:26.140
Does reincarnation exist?

11:26.141 --> 11:27.441
It does.

11:27.442 --> 11:29.544
As past human lives or as animals?

11:29.545 --> 11:31.379
- Both.
- Who have I been?

11:31.380 --> 11:33.214
- You were Henry the Eighth.
- Wow!

11:33.215 --> 11:36.083
Let me finish. You were Henry,
the eighth guy to have sex

11:36.084 --> 11:38.219
with Rock Hudson
at one of his pool parties.

11:38.220 --> 11:40.221
Aww.

11:40.222 --> 11:42.657
How many more shows is
John Stamos gonna get?

11:42.658 --> 11:46.594
- Zero.
- Good. That's... That's good.

11:50.666 --> 11:52.733
Are you real?

11:52.734 --> 11:54.402
Do you think I'm real, Peter?

11:54.403 --> 11:57.572
I like to believe there's
something bigger than me

11:57.573 --> 11:59.240
out there keeping a watch out.

11:59.241 --> 12:01.142
Different people think different things.

12:01.143 --> 12:02.910
I'm kind of like a nanny cam.

12:02.911 --> 12:04.946
<i>The idea that I may exist is enough</i>

12:04.947 --> 12:06.914
for some people to behave better.

12:06.915 --> 12:10.585
When I used to ask my mom
what God was, she would say,

12:10.586 --> 12:13.754
"God is love." I always liked that.

12:13.755 --> 12:15.156
That's nice, Peter.

12:15.157 --> 12:17.592
God and love are very similar concepts.

12:17.593 --> 12:19.760
- They come from the same place.
- Tatooine?

12:19.761 --> 12:23.431
<i>Ha! I always forget
you're such a Star Wars guy.</i>

12:25.000 --> 12:27.268
Man, when are they gonna fix
this elevator?

12:27.269 --> 12:30.871
It's not broken. I just haven't
decided where it's going yet.

12:34.109 --> 12:36.544
What's a "mezzanine"?

12:36.545 --> 12:38.946
- It's like a loge.
- What's a "loge"?

12:38.947 --> 12:40.781
Oh, hey, what's with all the questions?

12:40.782 --> 12:43.050
Yeah, you don't know either.

12:43.051 --> 12:44.518
W-Wait, hold on.

12:44.519 --> 12:48.055
- Am I... Am I dead?
- Yes.

12:48.056 --> 12:50.191
Oh, my God!

12:50.192 --> 12:52.526
Since you're now a ghost,
would you like to do pottery

12:52.527 --> 12:54.462
while straddling present-day Demi Moore?

12:54.463 --> 12:56.631
- Pass.
- Yeah.

12:56.632 --> 12:58.666
Not getting a lot of takers
for that one.

12:58.667 --> 13:00.534
I feel like the bones in her back

13:00.535 --> 13:02.470
would hurt my tummy.

13:05.320 --> 13:07.849
Am I... Am I really dead?

13:07.850 --> 13:09.030
Well, if you weren't dead,

13:09.031 --> 13:10.998
<i>would you feel nothing when I do this?</i>

13:10.999 --> 13:12.833
Ah! Son of a bitch!

13:12.834 --> 13:14.268
Oh, you know what?
That's right, it takes a day.

13:14.269 --> 13:15.569
M-My bad. Sorry.

13:15.570 --> 13:17.071
Tomorrow I do that, you feel nothing.

13:17.072 --> 13:18.406
But trust me, you're dead.

13:18.407 --> 13:20.374
But I can't be. Hold on, give me a sec.

13:23.845 --> 13:26.781
I can't be dead.
I have a family who needs me.

13:26.782 --> 13:28.382
Actually, Peter, from what I've seen,

13:28.383 --> 13:30.952
I think your family would be
better off without you.

13:30.953 --> 13:32.787
What? What do you mean?

13:32.788 --> 13:34.355
Well, you're an inattentive husband

13:34.356 --> 13:35.690
and a terrible parent.

13:35.691 --> 13:37.391
Oh, says Father of the Year.

13:37.392 --> 13:39.360
Oh, please. He played that
for all it was worth.

13:39.361 --> 13:41.028
"Why has thou forsaken me?"

13:41.029 --> 13:42.763
You know what? I did him a favor.

13:42.764 --> 13:44.532
Okay, well, th-there's a lot
to unpack there.

13:44.533 --> 13:46.801
But come on, God, you gotta
give me another chance.

13:46.802 --> 13:49.603
I'll show you how good a husband
and father I can be.

13:49.604 --> 13:52.039
Are you asking for a second chance?

13:52.040 --> 13:53.607
I-I guess so.

13:53.608 --> 13:56.544
Huh. No one's ever done that.

13:56.545 --> 13:58.212
You know what? You're on.

13:58.213 --> 14:00.047
I'll give you one day to prove to me

14:00.048 --> 14:01.983
that your family is better off
with you alive.

14:01.984 --> 14:05.119
I'll return you to your life
before you were in a coma.

14:05.120 --> 14:07.254
Thanks, God! I know I can do it.

14:07.255 --> 14:09.290
I've faced bigger challenges.

14:09.291 --> 14:12.093
Like when I recorded that
Russian language album.

14:14.062 --> 14:16.998
♪

14:32.581 --> 14:35.016
<i>♪ Vodka! ♪</i>

14:40.922 --> 14:44.325
Okay, kids. I know how you
always wanted kittens,

14:44.326 --> 14:46.193
so guess what I brought home?

14:46.194 --> 14:48.262
This very pregnant, about-to-burst,

14:48.263 --> 14:50.031
distended-nipples street cat.

14:52.934 --> 14:55.269
Peter, you can't bring home a feral cat.

14:55.270 --> 14:57.338
She doesn't want to be
around people right now.

14:57.339 --> 14:59.607
She needs a quiet space
to have her kittens.

14:59.608 --> 15:01.475
Yeah, so everyone gather 'round close.

15:01.476 --> 15:03.944
Her name is Sophie,
and she's fully dilated.

15:03.945 --> 15:05.780
Chris!

15:05.781 --> 15:08.282
She doesn't like that, but
I understand the instinct.

15:08.283 --> 15:10.818
Now, we all need to do our part
to help with the birth.

15:10.819 --> 15:12.453
Meg, boil some water.

15:12.454 --> 15:13.988
Brian, get some clean rags.

15:13.989 --> 15:15.389
Chris, blankets.

15:15.390 --> 15:17.158
Stewie, Band-Aids for me.

15:17.159 --> 15:19.126
Isn't it nice that we're
spending this time together

15:19.127 --> 15:20.628
as a family?

15:20.629 --> 15:23.931
Let's go spend it in the ER.

15:30.906 --> 15:33.841
Well, look at us.
Out for a fun family dinner.

15:33.842 --> 15:36.644
If anyone's watching, they'd
say, "Look at that family."

15:36.645 --> 15:38.312
Look how happy they are."

15:38.313 --> 15:40.581
Well, the kids do love Fuddruckers.

15:40.582 --> 15:42.516
Yeah, getting to design
any burger you want?

15:42.517 --> 15:45.052
Your only limit is your imagination.

15:45.053 --> 15:46.587
What kind you make there
for yourself, Chris?

15:46.588 --> 15:47.988
- Plain.
- Plain?

15:47.989 --> 15:49.590
What do you mean "plain"?

15:49.591 --> 15:51.992
It's a plain burger.
That's how I like them.

15:51.993 --> 15:54.495
That's not a burger,
that's just a meat sandwich.

15:54.496 --> 15:56.831
At least Meg went wild
and got a beige burger.

15:56.832 --> 15:58.332
No, I got chicken.

15:58.333 --> 16:00.868
What? Here? This is Fuddruckers.

16:00.869 --> 16:02.937
What... what part of Fuddruckers
don't you understand?

16:02.938 --> 16:04.238
All of it.

16:04.239 --> 16:05.406
All right, let's start this again.

16:05.407 --> 16:06.774
You're all gonna get up,

16:06.775 --> 16:08.909
go back up to that
toppings bar, and go nuts.

16:08.910 --> 16:10.911
But it tastes good like this.

16:10.912 --> 16:13.380
It's not supposed to taste good.
It's supposed to look crazy.

16:13.381 --> 16:14.548
What the hell are you doing?

16:14.549 --> 16:16.450
I'm cutting it. It's easier to eat.

16:16.451 --> 16:18.018
It's not supposed to be easy to eat.

16:18.019 --> 16:19.887
Half of it is supposed
to fall onto your plate

16:19.888 --> 16:22.256
when you squeeze it, and the
rest goes onto your shirt.

16:22.257 --> 16:23.591
How's everything going over here?

16:23.592 --> 16:25.192
Terrible! Go away!

16:25.193 --> 16:27.394
See, look, now I have to be
even more ridiculous

16:27.395 --> 16:29.396
to make up for what you guys
aren't doing.

16:29.397 --> 16:32.299
Silverware? Put them on.
Salt shaker? Whatever.

16:32.300 --> 16:34.368
Ice from soda, get on that burger.

16:34.369 --> 16:35.970
Peter, people are staring.

16:35.971 --> 16:38.105
Yeah, they're saying,
"Look at the creative guy.

16:38.106 --> 16:39.874
"Look at King Fuddrucker over there.

16:39.875 --> 16:41.575
"Usually you put a burger on a tray.

16:41.576 --> 16:43.978
This guy's putting a tray
on a (BLEEP) burger!"

16:43.979 --> 16:45.479
Are you through, Peter?

16:45.480 --> 16:47.214
Not yet, I'm not. Give me the car keys.

16:47.215 --> 16:50.184
- Peter...
- Give me... the car keys.

16:54.589 --> 16:56.290
That's Fuddruckers.

16:57.392 --> 16:58.959
Peter, you've opened the trunk.

16:58.960 --> 17:00.928
People are pulling things
out of our car.

17:00.929 --> 17:03.430
Good. That's also Fuddruckers...
Get used to it.

17:03.431 --> 17:05.833
And prepare to fish my teeth
out of my stool.

17:05.834 --> 17:08.402
- Peter, enough.
- You guys clearly don't get it.

17:08.403 --> 17:11.071
I'm sure when you explain
what we're supposed to get,

17:11.072 --> 17:12.406
we'll get it.

17:15.076 --> 17:17.678
Those poor kids. Those poor babies.

17:17.679 --> 17:19.947
Hey, Chris, what do you got there?

17:19.948 --> 17:21.315
A plain burger.

17:21.316 --> 17:23.217
Looks good.

17:27.255 --> 17:28.255
<i>You can do this, Peter.</i>

17:28.256 --> 17:29.623
<i>You love your family.</i>

17:29.624 --> 17:31.425
<i>You can do this, Peter,
you love your family.</i>

17:31.426 --> 17:33.761
<i>You can do this, Peter.
You love your family.</i>

17:33.762 --> 17:35.763
Dad, can you crack your window
a little bit?

17:35.764 --> 17:37.097
I hate you all so much!

17:37.098 --> 17:39.033
Uh-oh.

17:46.541 --> 17:48.442
♪

17:55.550 --> 17:56.717
Ah!

18:11.132 --> 18:12.499
Did you guys see that?

18:12.500 --> 18:14.802
The bunny rabbit family
you just ran over?

18:14.803 --> 18:16.737
Yeah. We all saw that, Peter.

18:16.738 --> 18:20.474
Come on, kids. Let's go inside.

18:20.475 --> 18:24.078
Before you go,
there's something I want to say.

18:24.079 --> 18:26.013
If anything were to happen to me, Lois,

18:26.014 --> 18:28.215
I'll miss you more than life...

18:28.216 --> 18:32.019
the cereal, but not the board
game, which I quite enjoy.

18:32.020 --> 18:34.021
- Okay.
- And Meg,

18:34.022 --> 18:35.422
I'm sorry I'll never get a chance

18:35.423 --> 18:38.058
to walk you down the aisle... at Costco,

18:38.059 --> 18:40.361
to furnish your sad,
single-lady apartment.

18:40.362 --> 18:42.529
- Thanks, Dad.
- And Stewie,

18:42.530 --> 18:46.667
it kills me that I'll never see
you become a man... loving twink.

18:46.668 --> 18:48.335
Is anyone gonna stop him?

18:48.336 --> 18:51.171
And, Chris, whenever you're
feeling defeated,

18:51.172 --> 18:54.842
<i>I want you to remember to always
reach for the Stars...</i>

18:54.843 --> 18:58.045
<i>Sky and Hutch DVD that fell
behind the entertainment center.</i>

18:58.046 --> 19:00.014
Sorry, you were the last one.

19:00.015 --> 19:01.915
- What about me?
- You're a dog.

19:01.916 --> 19:04.718
Peter, what's going on?
Why are you saying these things?

19:04.719 --> 19:07.121
Sorry. W-Why don't you guys go inside?

19:07.122 --> 19:09.256
I'm gonna stay out here and
listen to Nina Blackwood

19:09.257 --> 19:11.492
slowly die of throat cancer
on the radio.

19:13.461 --> 19:16.130
<i>Our next artist first climbed the charts</i>

19:16.131 --> 19:18.399
<i>with "Dancing With Myself."</i>

19:18.400 --> 19:23.070
<i>Of course, that artist is Billy Idol.</i>

19:23.071 --> 19:24.799
I'm supposed to get her

19:24.800 --> 19:27.308
a week from Thursday,
but I may be moving that up.

19:27.309 --> 19:30.277
I suppose you know why I'm here.

19:30.278 --> 19:32.313
Yeah. I guess so.

19:32.314 --> 19:34.248
It's weird. For the first seven days,

19:34.249 --> 19:36.784
all I did was create things,
but since then,

19:36.785 --> 19:38.319
it's just killing, killing, killing.

19:38.320 --> 19:39.953
Well, go ahead and do it.

19:39.954 --> 19:41.889
My family would be better off
without me.

19:41.890 --> 19:44.725
I'm a terrible husband
and a terrible father.

19:44.726 --> 19:46.393
I should never have questioned you.

19:46.394 --> 19:48.762
You were right about everything.

19:51.132 --> 19:52.466
Say that again.

19:52.467 --> 19:54.335
You were right about everything.

19:54.336 --> 19:56.503
That's all I needed to hear.

19:58.673 --> 19:59.973
That's what religion is.

19:59.974 --> 20:01.742
It's not about being good or bad.

20:01.743 --> 20:05.346
It's just blind subservience
to an imaginary being.

20:05.347 --> 20:07.247
So, I'm not gonna die?

20:07.248 --> 20:08.949
Nope, not for another four years.

20:08.950 --> 20:10.250
Thank you, God!

20:10.251 --> 20:13.821
Bless you, my child... pornography fan.

20:13.822 --> 20:15.189
You did it to me.

20:15.190 --> 20:17.691
- Can I use that one on my son?
- Sure.

20:19.127 --> 20:21.428
Hey, Chris, you like
pictures of naked children

20:21.429 --> 20:23.030
because you're gross and weird.

20:23.031 --> 20:25.032
Ah, he screwed it up.

20:31.170 --> 20:32.671
And I'm sorry about Fuddruckers.

20:32.672 --> 20:34.072
It won't happen again.

20:34.073 --> 20:37.342
Because nothing means more to me
than my family.

20:37.343 --> 20:40.779
Oh, Peter. That's wonderful.
What helped you come around?

20:40.780 --> 20:43.448
Well, Lois, let's just say
the big man upstairs

20:43.449 --> 20:46.017
put in a hard day's work today.

20:46.018 --> 20:49.387
Well, looks like quitting time.

20:49.388 --> 20:51.556
Good night, Kirk Cameron.

20:51.557 --> 20:53.525
See you tomorrow, Gene Rayburn.

20:53.526 --> 20:57.696
See you when the sun rises,
James Bro... Mamma mia!

20:57.697 --> 21:00.697
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru